---
import Frame from '../../components/PageFrame.astro';
const items = [
  {
    title: 'Coherent period filters',
    body: 'Switch week, month and quarter. Every dependent number, label, bar and row changes together.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Accessible trends',
    body: 'Read the exact values in an equivalent semantic table, with a text description of the chart.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Transparent demo datasets',
    body: 'Prepared fixtures make the arithmetic inspectable. Counts and snapshot metrics have distinct definitions.',
  },
];
---

<Frame label="Insights" items={items}>
  <section class="container section demo-section" id="demo-guide">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">TRY IT / ILLUSTRATIVE OPERATIONS</p>
      <h2>A dashboard you can check.</h2>
      <p>
        Change the period, inspect the total and open the underlying table. The
        figures are fictional local fixtures, designed to demonstrate consistent
        reporting interactions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">DEFINED BEFORE DESIGNED</p>
      <h2>Know what a number means.</h2>
      <p>
        Completed workflows is the sum of all completion counts for the selected
        sample period: 103 this week, 181 this month and 558 this quarter. The
        bars and the table use those same values.
      </p>
      <p>
        Awaiting review is a separate snapshot. Median duration is a prepared
        illustrative value; it cannot be calculated from daily completion
        counts. There is no previous-period dataset, so this dashboard makes no
        growth claim.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reading">
      <h3>A higher count is a question, not a conclusion.</h3>
      <p>
        More completed work could reflect a busier period, a different task mix
        or a changed definition. A chart alone cannot explain quality, workload
        or customer satisfaction.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before comparing two periods, check their duration, coverage and rules.
        Week, month and quarter in this demo have different lengths and are not
        directly comparable growth windows.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/journal/choosing-useful-dashboard-metrics/">
        Choose useful dashboard metrics →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section">
    <img
      class="diagram"
      src="/images/diagrams/insights-flow.svg"
      width="1200"
      height="340"
      loading="lazy"
      alt="Sample events move through a period filter and reconciliation into an accessible report."
    />
    <a class="text-link" href="/experience/">
      Explore the interface decisions →
    </a>
  </section>
</Frame>
